-- title:
--   Square polynomial presentations of the levels of a p-divisible group over mathcal O_K
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $p$ (as a `Fact`) and let $K$ be an intermediate field of $\mathbb Q_p$ inside the algebraic closure `PadicAlgCl p` which is finite-dimensional over $\mathbb Q_p$; write $\mathcal O_K =$ [`PadicAlgCl.ringOfIntegers p K`](def/PadicAlgCl_RingOfIntegers.html#L11) for the subalgebra of `PadicAlgCl p` over $\mathbb Z_p$ obtained as the intersection of the integral closure of $\mathbb Z_p$ in `PadicAlgCl p` with $K$ viewed as a $\mathbb Z_p$-subalgebra. Let $h$ be a natural number and let $G$ be a $p$-divisible group of height $h$ over $\mathcal O_K$ in the sense of the structure [`PDivisibleGroup`](def/PDivisibleGroup_Basic.html#L199): a family of commutative rings `G.level v`, each a cocommutative Hopf algebra over $\mathcal O_K$ that is finite and free as an $\mathcal O_K$-module of rank $p^{v h}$, together with surjective coalgebra–algebra maps `G.transition v : G.level (v+1) →ₐc[\mathcal O_K] G.level v` whose kernels are the ideals [`PDivisibleGroup.Hopf.torsionIdeal _ (G.level (v+1)) (p^v)`](def/PDivisibleGroup_Basic.html#L157), i.e. the images of the augmentation ideal under multiplication by $p^v$. The assertion is that for every $v$ there exist a natural number $m$ and a family $f : \mathrm{Fin}\,m \to \mathcal O_K[X_1,\dots,X_m]$ of $m$ polynomials in $m$ variables such that the quotient of $\mathcal O_K[X_1,\dots,X_m]$ by the ideal generated by the range of $f$ admits an $\mathcal O_K$-algebra isomorphism onto `G.level v` (stated as nonemptiness of the type of such isomorphisms).
--
--   This says that each level of a $p$-divisible group over the ring of integers of a finite extension of $\mathbb Q_p$ is a relative global complete intersection over $\mathcal O_K$, presented by as many equations as variables — the integral counterpart of the fact that finite flat group schemes over a complete discrete valuation ring are syntomic. The square presentation is what makes the discriminant of a level accessible, and it is used in [`PDivisibleGroup.associated_discr_level_of_hasDimension_of_ringOfIntegers`](thm.html#PDivisibleGroup.associated_discr_level_of_hasDimension_of_ringOfIntegers).
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_PDivisibleGroup_exists_square_presentation_level_of_ringOfIntegers.lean

